  "contract": [
    "Drain pointer messages from the existing BLE queue with timeout0 and no priority output. A successful null dequeue returns immediately without free; every processed nonnull item, including unknown events, is freed once before reloading the live queue handle. The passed output pointer cell is cleared between receives as stock does.",
    "Event2 cancels the exact empty legacy callback and time callback, schedules slow parameters, then reads the live role byte. Phone role uses the existing control byte and Nordic pm_conn_secure(false), tolerates success/busy17 and preserves the distinct follow-up arguments/delays. Glasses role preserves target gating, cached state/status reports, transmit-power and unbind scheduling.",
    "Events16/32/64 call the existing parameter adapter with modes1/2/0. Event8 forwards one byte when the full uint32 length word is nonzero, with argument length1 and trailing0.",
    "Event200 retains the cached glasses handle, freshly checked length and cleared8-byte address query span. It accepts a match against either six-byte target, schedules a mismatch disconnect at raw0x5000, stores both targets regardless of query result/length gate, then selects advertising from mismatch and role occupancy.",
    "Event4000 logs and supplies the same target pointer to both store arguments. Diagnostics preserve the native event200 second-target read despite its right-target label. Message words/bytes are reloaded at their observed logging/provider boundaries.",
    "The empty callback at0x4e1e2 is a literal two-byte BX LR function in stock. The shared exported C empty function compiles to those two bytes and supplies one canonical scheduler key; no timeout work is invented."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The broad consumer import closes, exposing eight real lower hardware/service dependencies instead of supplying fake success implementations. Application imports therefore rise from72 to79; this is not a final application link.",
    "Replay buffers have readable native header and route-specific payload extents: pair/op8 need one byte, event200 twelve bytes and event4000 six. Header-length edge cases are compared only with sufficiently backed buffers. Native faults/overreads from short allocated or invalid pointers are not a supported C contract.",
    "The parameter integration executes actual C mode/slow/control helpers, GAP table/profile ownership and SDK SVC gateway instructions. Supervisor results, security/provider services, logging, scheduler, target/state/advertising backends and queue-get are models.",
    "The producer integration executes the existing C encoder, memory movement, consumer and parameter helpers with a prepared allocator/FIFO/notification backend. It checks successful allocation/queueing and failed allocation/queue insertion ownership; it does not execute the RTOS allocator/queue kernel or physical radio.",
    "The empty callback is passed to cancellation by identity in these consumer replays. Its two-byte code equality is a narrow body observation, not final image integration or a reconstruction-wide byte-identity claim.",
    "Ordinary void AAPCS behavior, callee-saved integer/FP registers, masks, stack guards, observable passed buffers and callback tokens are checked. Private stack addresses, incidental caller-clobbered returns, aliases/concurrency, arbitrary malformed allocations and physical timing are excluded.",
    "R1 manifest check passes. Global sources-check retains the unrelated unlisted G2 resident_rom_thumb_set.S. Final placement and device boot remain unverified. Byte identity and a paid compiler are not requirements."
  ],
